From: ImWebBrowser
Subject: [PATCH] WPE: allow sharing the host network with the web process for
 WebRTC/ICE (WEBKIT_ENABLE_NETWORK_ACCESS)

The bubblewrap sandbox (ENABLE_BUBBLEWRAP_SANDBOX=ON) launches the web
process with --unshare-net unless remote inspector support is enabled
(BubblewrapLauncher::shouldUnshareNetwork). GTK already exempts its web
process from --unshare-net when X11 runs over TCP, but the WPE port has
no such exception, so on WPE the web process always lands in its own
network namespace where only loopback exists.

The WPE web process performs its own WebRTC/ICE candidate gathering (via
GstWebRTC + libnice). With only loopback visible it can enumerate no real
interface, emits no host ICE candidates, and real-time peers (e.g. GeForce
Now) can never establish a connection (error 0xC0F2220E).

Mirror the GTK behaviour and let the WPE web process share the host
network when the user opts in via the WEBKIT_ENABLE_NETWORK_ACCESS
environment variable, keeping the sandbox isolated by default.

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp
@@ -717,6 +717,21 @@ static bool shouldUnshareNetwork(ProcessLauncher::ProcessType processType, char
     if (remoteInspectorEnabled())
         return false;
 
+#if PLATFORM(WPE)
+    // The WPE web process performs its own WebRTC/ICE candidate gathering (via
+    // GstWebRTC + libnice), which needs to enumerate the host network interfaces
+    // to produce host candidates. GTK already exempts its web process from
+    // --unshare-net for X11-over-TCP below; the WPE port has no such exception,
+    // so the web process is dropped into a netns with only loopback. libnice then
+    // sees no real interface, emits no host candidates, and real-time peers
+    // (e.g. GeForce Now) can never connect (0xC0F2220E). Let the WPE web process
+    // share the host network when opted in, keeping the sandbox isolated by
+    // default.
+    if (processType == ProcessLauncher::ProcessType::Web
+        && g_getenv("WEBKIT_ENABLE_NETWORK_ACCESS"))
+        return false;
+#endif
+
     // xdg-dbus-proxy needs access to host abstract sockets to connect to the a11y bus. Secure
     // host services must not use abstract sockets.
     if (processType == ProcessLauncher::ProcessType::DBusProxy)
